🌡️ Temperature Converter – Web Application
📌 Objective
The goal of this project is to build a simple and interactive Temperature Converter web application that allows users to convert temperatures between Celsius, Fahrenheit, and Kelvin. The project focuses on implementing conversion logic using JavaScript and providing a clean, user-friendly interface using HTML and CSS.

🧩 Steps Performed
1.Created HTML Structure (index.html)
Added a title “Temperature Converter” and an input field for users to enter the temperature value.
Included two dropdown menus to select the conversion units: “From” and “To”.
Added a Convert button to trigger the conversion process.
Displayed the conversion result dynamically below the button.

2.Implemented Styling (style.css)
Designed a light blue theme for a modern and calm interface.
Styled input fields, dropdowns, and buttons for better visibility and usability.
Ensured the layout is centered and responsive for all screen sizes.

3.Added Functionality (script.js)
Used JavaScript to handle user input, perform temperature conversions, and display the results dynamically.
Supported conversions among:
Celsius ↔ Fahrenheit
Celsius ↔ Kelvin
Fahrenheit ↔ Kelvin

4.Tested the Application
Verified all possible conversion combinations for accuracy.
Ensured the result updates instantly after clicking the “Convert” button.
🛠️ Tools & Technologies Used

HTML5 – For creating the webpage structure.
CSS3 – For styling and layout (light blue theme).
JavaScript (ES6) – For implementing temperature conversion logic.
Visual Studio Code – As the development environment.

🎯 Outcome
A fully functional, responsive Temperature Converter Web App that provides instant and accurate temperature conversions.
Simple UI with easy-to-use dropdown menus and a clear result display.
Demonstrates the integration of HTML, CSS, and JavaScript for an interactive web project.
